          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "According to the school's own figures, BIS Hanoi (British International School Hanoi) graduates were accepted by more than 300 universities around the world between 2016 and 2024.\n\n**UK (the most common destination)**\n- University of Cambridge\n- Imperial College London\n- UCL (University College London)\n- King's College London\n- London School of Economics (LSE)\n- University of Manchester, University of Bristol and University of Warwick\n\nThe school notes that most of these are Russell Group universities ranked in the QS UK Top 10 for 2024.\n\n**USA**\n- Stanford University\n- Yale University\n- UC Berkeley\n\n**Australia and Canada**\n- University of Sydney\n- University of Melbourne\n- University of Toronto\n\n**Asia**\n- Hong Kong: University of Hong Kong (HKU) and Hong Kong University of Science and Technology (HKUST)\n- Singapore: National University of Singapore (NUS) and Nanyang Technological University (NTU)\n- South Korea: Korea University, Yonsei University and KAIST\n\nAll of this comes from the school's website, so it shows its best results. It lists where students were accepted, which isn't necessarily where they enrolled, and it doesn't say how many students got into each university. The school's University Destinations page has more detailed lists you can download, including the Class of 2024 results, QS Top 200 global universities and US Top 100 schools: https://www.nordangliaeducation.com/bis-hanoi/academic-excellence/university-destinations\n\nIf you want to know how typical students do, rather than the top results, you could ask the admissions office for a full list of where the last few graduating classes enrolled."
